  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>34</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> long ladder weighing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> leans on a frictionless wall. Its feet rest on the floor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> away from the wall as shown in the figure. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></math> are the reaction forces of the floor and the wall, then ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mfrac></math> will be :<br />(Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>.)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6a305d3f-238a-4aa4-bece-92bd34152a39-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 220px;\" /></p>",
